 "verdict": "VERIFIED 18.49 (score 93.28), held out 23.45 (docs/concepts/verify/slipper-nose-knuckle-3r.py; ledger WATCH) - a Pareto move of the lead, not a reach move. The roller is deleted and the flank re-fit at the honest friction (mu 0.087, PA_kin 38): frozen exact Bench(110,360) 18.49 (score 93.28) vs the lead roller's 18.67 through the same Frozen class. Same reach (261/360, overhead 8/28) and the same 2 contact poses; +0.0018 in-band from the re-cut arm. Complexity 22.25 vs 24.25 at screening (18.25 vs 20.25 since the 2026-10-17 knee-loop record fix), one bought bearing fewer, 0 passive translations. With the lead's drive left unchanged the nose costs +0.10 at mu 0.05 and +1.23 at mu 0.087; the re-fit flank holds its fast number to mu 0.12. The +0.18 is below the 1-point rule: claim it as a simplification at equal score, not as a new lead by points. Kneeless + wedge control reproduced (21.18 flat / 20.12 wedged at mu 0.05; 21.76 / 20.70 at 0.087). The planar wedge cannot drop on the pin-knee lead (hub 3 already passes 0.38 mm over the skin at a fit pose).",
